Z||000004||stimpy||03-18-2001||12:38 PM||||I'm not gonna say avoid ACE like bubonic plague, but I'd say explore ALL other options before sending your car to Colorado for a 3.8 swap.<BR>Make sure the shop you use will acually engineer the swap. Things to look for: Some kind of accomidation for a torque strut so yor alt. does not gouge out the hood, break the exhaust, and cause tranny failure.<BR>Also relocation of the coil packs so they are not cooked over they exhaust manifold.<P>I'd also recommend that you get Chris West's 3.8headers that allow you to retain stock Fiero exhaust. ACE's system does not allow for a muffler. Imagine 2200 rpm at 80 MPH with no muffler. Can you say headache? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||03-18-2001||02:20 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.thefieroshop.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefieroshop.com</A>  does 3800 swaps, they're in Toronto... I haven't had any work done by them, but I hear they're pretty good. Nice people too, I met the owner at a show last fall.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||14
